1
00:00:35,076 --> 00:00:37,037
Mikoy and I are getting married

2
00:00:42,041 --> 00:00:44,127
I even tried to invite you.

3
00:00:44,210 --> 00:00:46,087
If you don't want to come, then don't.

4
00:00:51,551 --> 00:00:54,679
Now is the perfect time
to introduce you online.

5
00:00:54,763 --> 00:00:57,474
That's why I want to officially

6
00:00:57,557 --> 00:01:01,686
launch your love team on your wedding day.

7
00:01:01,770 --> 00:01:02,604
You know what?

8
00:01:02,687 --> 00:01:05,732
Let's see if you
can convince Chiara first. Okay?

9
00:01:07,233 --> 00:01:10,236
Have you ever been a maid of honor before?

10
00:01:11,780 --> 00:01:12,947
Then that's perfect.

11
00:01:14,908 --> 00:01:17,368
You're the perfect
maid of honor for Chiara.

12
00:01:17,452 --> 00:01:21,331
Maybe this is an opportunity
for me to get closer to Chiara.

13
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:25,251
And make sure she doesn't
go back to her old ways.

14
00:01:25,335 --> 00:01:28,421
You must be missing
all your fun with Angelito.

15
00:01:28,505 --> 00:01:30,715
Of course I really miss it.

16
00:01:30,799 --> 00:01:33,426
He reminds me of the life
Angelito and I had in Cebu.

17
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:40,350
Is this true, Quintin?

18
00:01:43,394 --> 00:01:47,148
I can't blame my friend for thinking that,

19
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:50,485
but this is all a misunderstanding.

20
00:01:52,237 --> 00:01:53,905
How is it a misunderstanding?

21
00:01:55,949 --> 00:01:57,992
I filed for personal leave.

22
00:01:58,076 --> 00:02:01,871
You know, whenever I'm on vacation,
I go on DND,

23
00:02:01,955 --> 00:02:04,207
or "Do Not Disturb".

24
00:02:04,290 --> 00:02:06,459
That's the trend these days,
which is why you couldn't reach me.

25
00:02:07,335 --> 00:02:09,671
As for the budget,

26
00:02:09,754 --> 00:02:12,090
it was missing one signatory.

27
00:02:13,508 --> 00:02:14,968
That's why the release was delayed.

28
00:02:15,844 --> 00:02:17,512
You know how it is.

29
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:21,015
One signature can create a ripple effect
on important matters.

30
00:02:26,813 --> 00:02:32,068
Then how do you explain
the evidence linking you

31
00:02:33,236 --> 00:02:35,029
to the Sinigang Cartel?

32
00:02:36,531 --> 00:02:39,450
These days, everything can be manipulated.

33
00:02:39,534 --> 00:02:40,702
Because of technology.

34
00:02:40,785 --> 00:02:42,370
It's AI.

35
00:02:42,453 --> 00:02:46,207
Even Viber conversations
can be AI-generated.

36
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:48,877
Oh, yes. AI?

37
00:02:50,670 --> 00:02:51,546
I can relate to that AI thing.

38
00:02:51,629 --> 00:02:55,717
I remember one time I was in Hawaii,
traveling alone.

39
00:02:58,303 --> 00:03:02,056
Then suddenly, photos came out
showing me with IT girls!

40
00:03:08,605 --> 00:03:09,898
But were they pretty?

41
00:03:09,981 --> 00:03:11,941
Yes, they were bea--

42
00:03:12,025 --> 00:03:13,484
The beaches.

43
00:03:13,568 --> 00:03:16,362
The beaches in Hawaii
are absolutely beautiful.

44
00:03:19,324 --> 00:03:22,535
That was obviously AI,
just like what happened to me.

45
00:03:23,202 --> 00:03:27,290
And I'm almost certain
the Concordat was behind it

46
00:03:27,373 --> 00:03:33,421
because they know I'm helping dismantle
their organization here in our country.

47
00:03:36,382 --> 00:03:40,762
That's why they're trying to destroy me
and tear our friendship apart, my friend.

48
00:03:48,686 --> 00:03:51,105
You wouldn't let my haters get to you.

49
00:03:51,189 --> 00:03:53,816
And you wouldn't let them ruin me

50
00:03:53,900 --> 00:03:56,402
or destroy our friendship, right?

51
00:03:57,111 --> 00:03:58,696
You're right, my friend.

52
00:04:00,740 --> 00:04:01,783
It's okay.

53
00:04:06,579 --> 00:04:08,790
All right, then, meeting adjourned.

54
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,626
But Norberto, stay for a moment.

55
00:04:11,709 --> 00:04:14,587
- We need to discuss some other matters.
- Okay.

56
00:04:14,671 --> 00:04:16,089
- Mr. President.
- All right, Quintin.

57
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:17,465
- My friend.
- My friend.

58
00:04:17,548 --> 00:04:18,675
See you.

59
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:21,552
GLOBAL AGENCY FOR GOVERNMENT OPERATIONS

60
00:04:27,684 --> 00:04:31,396
Are you sure you're not going
to investigate Senator Quintin?

61
00:04:34,649 --> 00:04:36,150
Norberto.

62
00:04:37,235 --> 00:04:40,613
One thing I've learned
through all my years in office is,

63
00:04:41,197 --> 00:04:42,949
keep your friends close,

64
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,160
keep your enemies closer.

65
00:04:48,288 --> 00:04:55,128
You'll gather much stronger evidence
if he believes you still trust him.

66
00:04:57,964 --> 00:05:00,300
By the way, about the agency's budget,

67
00:05:00,383 --> 00:05:01,759
there have been some changes.

68
00:05:02,510 --> 00:05:03,970
You and Quintin can discuss it.

69
00:05:04,804 --> 00:05:07,307
Yes, Mr. President. Thank you.

70
00:05:30,455 --> 00:05:32,373
Good morning, everyone!

71
00:05:34,125 --> 00:05:36,711
Albay!

72
00:06:03,946 --> 00:06:05,531
<i>My dearest love.</i>

73
00:06:10,078 --> 00:06:13,706
<i>But I'm sorry I wasn't beside you</i>
<i>when you woke up.</i>

74
00:06:14,832 --> 00:06:16,417
<i>I didn't wake you up</i>

75
00:06:16,501 --> 00:06:20,088
<i>because I know you need</i>
<i>the extra hours of sleep,</i>

76
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:23,049
<i>especially with how busy</i>
<i>you've been lately,</i>

77
00:06:23,132 --> 00:06:26,844
<i>but I cooked you a meal</i>
<i>so that when you wake up,</i>

78
00:06:26,928 --> 00:06:30,681
<i>you'll still feel</i>
<i>just how much I love you.</i>

79
00:06:39,190 --> 00:06:40,525
Nice, huh?

80
00:06:52,245 --> 00:06:53,746
<i>Before you eat,</i>

81
00:06:53,830 --> 00:06:56,874
<i>finish reading the letter</i>
<i>I wrote for you first.</i>

82
00:07:05,591 --> 00:07:07,593
<i>As soon as you're done with work,</i>

83
00:07:07,677 --> 00:07:09,887
<i>can you please buy the groceries?</i>

84
00:07:09,971 --> 00:07:12,265
<i>I'm running low on supplies.</i>

85
00:07:12,348 --> 00:07:16,185
<i>I might get home late because</i>
<i>we have a big Korean tour group</i>

86
00:07:16,269 --> 00:07:18,438
<i>that we need to take care of.</i>

87
00:07:18,521 --> 00:07:20,064
<i>I love you, my love.</i>

88
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:22,233
I love you too, my love.

89
00:07:22,316 --> 00:07:23,359
No problem!

90
00:07:23,443 --> 00:07:25,194
I got this!

91
00:07:26,529 --> 00:07:29,991
<i>Don't say "No problem" or "I got this,"</i>

92
00:07:30,074 --> 00:07:33,077
<i>only to forget what I asked you to do.</i>

93
00:07:36,038 --> 00:07:37,665
Oh, sweetheart.

94
00:07:37,748 --> 00:07:39,792
Of course I won't forget that!

95
00:07:39,876 --> 00:07:41,794
Never! You know me!

96
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:46,883
<i>Actually, remember when I asked</i>
<i>you to buy a pineapple</i>

97
00:07:46,966 --> 00:07:49,010
<i>at the market the other day?</i>

98
00:07:49,093 --> 00:07:52,346
<i>And then you forgot to buy it?</i>

99
00:07:53,347 --> 00:07:57,727
<i>How can I call the dish pineapple chicken</i>
<i>without any pineapple?</i>

100
00:07:58,311 --> 00:08:01,606
Come on, sweetheart.
It only happened once.

101
00:08:05,818 --> 00:08:08,070
<i>It has happened many times,</i>

102
00:08:08,154 --> 00:08:10,948
<i>and this paper doesn't have enough space</i>

103
00:08:11,032 --> 00:08:13,576
<i>to list every single time</i>

104
00:08:13,659 --> 00:08:16,704
<i>you forgot to do what I asked you to do.</i>

105
00:08:20,166 --> 00:08:26,589
<i>Do not, under any circumstances,</i>
<i>forget to buy the groceries!</i>

106
00:08:26,672 --> 00:08:28,090
<i>Because if you do…</i>

107
00:08:31,385 --> 00:08:33,179
<i>Here's the grocery list.</i>

108
00:08:33,763 --> 00:08:34,972
And you still forgot it!

109
00:08:35,056 --> 00:08:37,225
Why did you forget it?

110
00:08:38,726 --> 00:08:39,602
Ow.

111
00:08:42,772 --> 00:08:45,483
I told you I needed the groceries!

112
00:08:47,401 --> 00:08:52,031
Okay, okay, okay! I promise I won't
forget the groceries. Groceries.

113
00:08:52,615 --> 00:08:54,575
I said groceries!
That's all you had to do!

114
00:08:54,659 --> 00:08:56,702
Ouch! Groceries. Ow!

115
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:04,585
I won't forget the groceries.

116
00:09:12,677 --> 00:09:13,970
Delicious, sweetheart.

117
00:09:23,312 --> 00:09:24,522
You're getting married.

118
00:09:25,106 --> 00:09:26,232
Lucky you.

119
00:09:26,315 --> 00:09:28,067
This one beside me…

120
00:09:28,150 --> 00:09:29,735
We've known each other for so long,

121
00:09:29,819 --> 00:09:33,281
and I've never seen you fall for anyone.

122
00:09:33,864 --> 00:09:34,824
That's true!

123
00:09:35,324 --> 00:09:37,159
- As if.
- Jan-Jan.

124
00:09:38,077 --> 00:09:39,328
Seriously.

125
00:09:39,412 --> 00:09:40,580
Let me ask you something.

126
00:09:41,330 --> 00:09:42,582
Do you already like someone?

127
00:09:45,751 --> 00:09:47,086
You know, Captain Pepe.

128
00:09:47,628 --> 00:09:48,462
I do.

129
00:09:49,755 --> 00:09:51,465
Really?

130
00:09:51,549 --> 00:09:53,426
You're just too dense.

131
00:09:56,053 --> 00:09:57,555
You're such a joker!

132
00:09:57,638 --> 00:09:59,974
You can't out-joke me. We're best buddies!

133
00:10:00,057 --> 00:10:01,684
You're unbelievable.

134
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:03,227
But, Mikoy.

135
00:10:03,853 --> 00:10:06,564
We've been drinking for quite a while now,

136
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:08,733
and you keep saying "groceries".

137
00:10:09,859 --> 00:10:11,235
Who is this "groceries"?

138
00:10:11,319 --> 00:10:14,030
Yes, who's this Rosary?

139
00:10:14,113 --> 00:10:15,823
Rosaline?

140
00:10:19,076 --> 00:10:21,454
- You're really drunk.
- Groceries.

141
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:25,499
Chiara just kept
reminding me over and over

142
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:28,419
not to forget her groceries.

143
00:10:28,502 --> 00:10:30,254
As if I'd forget them.

144
00:10:30,338 --> 00:10:31,422
Right?

145
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:32,923
Oh, that's what you meant.

146
00:10:33,007 --> 00:10:34,842
Groceries.

147
00:10:35,509 --> 00:10:37,470
You should've said that earlier!

148
00:10:39,680 --> 00:10:40,931
Wait.

149
00:10:41,015 --> 00:10:42,975
How far is the grocery store again?

150
00:10:46,562 --> 00:10:47,938
Far away!

151
00:10:50,691 --> 00:10:51,567
We're doomed.

152
00:10:52,735 --> 00:10:53,653
Come on!

153
00:10:55,363 --> 00:10:56,989
Where are we going?

154
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:19,887
Looks like we can't count
on our friend anymore.

155
00:11:38,239 --> 00:11:39,949
About our group work later, okay?

156
00:11:40,032 --> 00:11:41,283
Sure, bye!

157
00:11:46,539 --> 00:11:48,040
The day's barely started,

158
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:51,710
but you already look like
you're ready to go home.

159
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:52,753
What's wrong?

160
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:59,051
I just can't think of anything
to write for this reflection paper.

161
00:12:00,761 --> 00:12:04,306
Is that all? Come on. You've got this!

162
00:12:05,683 --> 00:12:09,353
Or maybe you just need
a little inspiration.

163
00:12:11,522 --> 00:12:15,025
You know what? You're right.
I can do this.

164
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:18,154
It's just a reflection paper.

165
00:12:18,863 --> 00:12:20,364
I'm Luisa Mae.

166
00:12:20,448 --> 00:12:23,117
The all-arounder Luisa Mae, right?

167
00:12:24,660 --> 00:12:25,703
<i>It's just a gun.</i>

168
00:12:29,081 --> 00:12:31,709
I won't die without putting up a fight.

169
00:12:37,298 --> 00:12:39,508
Are you impressed because I'm fearless?

170
00:12:42,720 --> 00:12:43,554
Yes!

171
00:12:44,180 --> 00:12:47,975
We should be ready to face
our schoolwork head-on, right?

172
00:12:48,058 --> 00:12:50,394
Our grades depend on it.

173
00:12:50,478 --> 00:12:53,272
And it's how we'll graduate.

174
00:12:53,355 --> 00:12:54,356
Right?

175
00:13:03,782 --> 00:13:05,242
You got this!

176
00:13:15,461 --> 00:13:18,756
Yes!

177
00:13:24,762 --> 00:13:25,804
Ouch.

178
00:13:30,267 --> 00:13:33,103
Chiara's going to kill me.

179
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:34,939
Mikoy.

180
00:13:35,022 --> 00:13:35,898
Mikoy!

181
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:38,943
Mikoy! What's happening to you?

182
00:13:39,026 --> 00:13:41,278
If the grocery store's closed,
we can go tomorrow.

183
00:13:41,362 --> 00:13:43,155
- Exactly.
- No way!

184
00:13:43,239 --> 00:13:45,366
Chiara made me promise

185
00:13:45,449 --> 00:13:48,285
I can't go home without the groceries.

186
00:13:48,369 --> 00:13:50,621
She'll seriously kill me.

187
00:13:50,704 --> 00:13:52,122
- I see.
- You're not even married yet,

188
00:13:52,206 --> 00:13:54,041
and you're already whipped?

189
00:13:54,124 --> 00:13:55,543
That's not being whipped.

190
00:13:55,626 --> 00:13:57,753
- That's called love, right?
- Exactly!

191
00:13:57,836 --> 00:13:59,797
All right, I'm heading there now,

192
00:13:59,880 --> 00:14:02,508
but why are you so terrified
just because we missed the groceries?

193
00:14:02,591 --> 00:14:04,593
- Yes.
- You know Chiara, right?

194
00:14:04,677 --> 00:14:05,970
When she gets mad,

195
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:07,763
the only part of your body
that isn't bruised is your eyes.

196
00:14:09,473 --> 00:14:10,558
Don't worry, Mikoy.

197
00:14:11,267 --> 00:14:12,643
That's what friends are for.

198
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:15,271
We'll protect you.

199
00:14:15,354 --> 00:14:16,188
- That's right.
- Yes.

200
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,940
Before you get hurt,

201
00:14:18,607 --> 00:14:19,775
- we'll take the hit first.
- We'll take the hit first.

202
00:14:24,113 --> 00:14:25,281
- Chiara!
- Chiara!

203
00:14:29,869 --> 00:14:31,036
- Chiara!
- Chiara!

204
00:14:31,120 --> 00:14:32,079
Chiara!

205
00:14:37,501 --> 00:14:38,419
What's this?

206
00:14:39,920 --> 00:14:42,006
You even brought your backup squad?

207
00:14:43,507 --> 00:14:47,136
Sweetheart, there's something
I want to tell you.

208
00:14:49,555 --> 00:14:51,056
I'll handle this.

209
00:14:53,434 --> 00:14:54,268
Chiara.

210
00:14:55,144 --> 00:14:57,021
We weren't able to buy groceries because…

211
00:14:57,104 --> 00:14:57,938
We were drinking.

212
00:14:58,022 --> 00:14:59,106
That's right.

213
00:15:00,399 --> 00:15:03,277
And we're here to protect Mikoy.

214
00:15:04,403 --> 00:15:06,322
Protect him?

215
00:15:08,866 --> 00:15:11,577
Chiara.

216
00:15:12,828 --> 00:15:14,163
So if you're angry,

217
00:15:14,872 --> 00:15:16,415
or if you're mad,

218
00:15:17,249 --> 00:15:18,626
take it all out on us first!

219
00:15:18,709 --> 00:15:20,920
- On us!
- On us!

220
00:15:24,924 --> 00:15:26,258
Are you sure?

221
00:15:26,342 --> 00:15:27,593
We're sure.

222
00:15:28,677 --> 00:15:30,512
- Dekyo?
- Absolutely!

223
00:15:31,430 --> 00:15:33,599
- Jan-Jan?
- Of course!

224
00:15:35,476 --> 00:15:37,561
Are you really sure

225
00:15:37,645 --> 00:15:44,276
that I'm going to take out
all my anger on all of you?

226
00:15:44,360 --> 00:15:45,361
All of us!

227
00:15:45,444 --> 00:15:47,363
- All of us!
- Yes!

228
00:15:47,446 --> 00:15:50,407
You mean all of it?

229
00:15:51,492 --> 00:15:52,743
- Every bit of it!
- As in every bit of it!

230
00:15:52,826 --> 00:15:53,661
Everything.

231
00:15:55,871 --> 00:15:56,789
You're dead!

232
00:15:56,872 --> 00:15:57,915
You're dead, Mikoy!

233
00:15:57,998 --> 00:16:00,167
You're on your own, Mikoy!

234
00:16:00,250 --> 00:16:01,794
You're dead, Mikoy!

235
00:16:01,877 --> 00:16:03,712
Be prepared for a black eye!

236
00:16:05,089 --> 00:16:06,590
Sweetheart, I'm really sorry!

237
00:16:06,674 --> 00:16:08,676
I swear, all day long,

238
00:16:08,759 --> 00:16:10,260
I kept reminding myself to buy groceries.

239
00:16:10,344 --> 00:16:11,470
But

240
00:16:12,596 --> 00:16:13,764
we just didn't make it in time.

241
00:16:13,847 --> 00:16:16,016
Turns out the grocery store
is so far away, sweetheart!

242
00:16:18,519 --> 00:16:19,395
I'm sorry.

243
00:16:20,396 --> 00:16:21,814
We can deal with that later.

244
00:16:24,024 --> 00:16:26,568
I just wanted to tell you
that you have a visitor.

245
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,694
I'm sorry.

246
00:17:08,777 --> 00:17:11,655
We didn't even get the chance
to say goodbye.

247
00:17:11,739 --> 00:17:14,825
Everything happened so fast

248
00:17:14,908 --> 00:17:16,493
after the La Morte Bianca incident.

249
00:17:18,412 --> 00:17:20,831
I understand
why you had to leave in a hurry.

250
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:24,501
And I'm glad you both settled here
in Albay so quickly.

251
00:17:26,003 --> 00:17:29,298
You know, you should stay here with us.

252
00:17:29,882 --> 00:17:31,925
It's just the two of us in this house.

253
00:17:32,968 --> 00:17:35,429
No, thanks. I've already
booked a hotel in town.

254
00:17:35,512 --> 00:17:36,722
I'll just stay there.

255
00:17:38,348 --> 00:17:40,476
By the way,
congratulations to you and Mikoy.

256
00:17:46,440 --> 00:17:47,900
I'm sorry too.

257
00:17:49,109 --> 00:17:51,820
For putting you in this situation.

258
00:17:51,904 --> 00:17:54,948
I just thought that,
of all people, you would understand.

259
00:17:59,536 --> 00:18:02,456
I've struggled with that my whole life.

260
00:18:04,875 --> 00:18:09,296
Because whenever I get annoyed
with someone I meet,

261
00:18:09,880 --> 00:18:13,425
I sometimes just want to snap their neck.

262
00:18:16,303 --> 00:18:18,972
You know, I feel the same way.

263
00:18:20,432 --> 00:18:23,060
That's why when I got your offer,

264
00:18:24,853 --> 00:18:26,188
I thought,

265
00:18:26,271 --> 00:18:29,233
I might never get another chance
to be someone's maid of honor.

266
00:18:37,074 --> 00:18:39,618
It's hard for me to make real friends too.

267
00:18:39,701 --> 00:18:45,124
Besides, I get irritated by idiots.

268
00:18:50,796 --> 00:18:54,591
I wonder how you managed to last
as Mikoy's handler.

269
00:18:55,717 --> 00:18:58,846
Hey, I can hear you! I'm right here.

270
00:18:59,596 --> 00:19:01,890
Be quiet over there.
I don't want to hear a word from you.

271
00:19:03,100 --> 00:19:04,017
See?

272
00:19:04,101 --> 00:19:05,978
That's how I talk to him.

273
00:19:10,524 --> 00:19:11,650
By the way,

274
00:19:12,234 --> 00:19:14,069
let's start planning
your bachelorette party.

275
00:19:14,778 --> 00:19:16,655
How many male dancers
do you want us to hire?

276
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:19,783
I know a place.

277
00:19:21,285 --> 00:19:24,037
You know, I kind of like that idea!

278
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:26,206
I think I want them to have six-packs!

279
00:19:26,290 --> 00:19:27,207
Six-packs.

280
00:19:27,291 --> 00:19:32,421
My future husband doesn't even have one.

281
00:19:35,507 --> 00:19:37,217
You two are just messing with me.

282
00:19:37,301 --> 00:19:38,385
It's fine. I'm okay with it.

283
00:19:38,969 --> 00:19:40,804
As long as you're having fun.

284
00:19:40,888 --> 00:19:42,222
I'm fine over here.

285
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:43,265
Go ahead.

286
00:19:43,348 --> 00:19:45,017
- Sweetheart.
- No!

287
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:47,186
I'm obviously just kidding!

288
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,395
Don't be so sensitive!

289
00:19:48,478 --> 00:19:52,274
- It's okay that you don't have one, right?
- No!

290
00:19:52,357 --> 00:19:56,069
You know, I'm just really excited
that Alex is here.

291
00:19:58,155 --> 00:20:00,449
And I'm excited to be your maid of honor.

292
00:20:01,033 --> 00:20:05,454
I'll make sure you're the most
special bride on your wedding day.

293
00:20:08,165 --> 00:20:10,959
By the way, I have
one more small gift for you.

294
00:20:14,463 --> 00:20:17,299
Isn't it a little early
to be giving gifts?

295
00:20:20,010 --> 00:20:21,887
Someone once told me

296
00:20:23,513 --> 00:20:26,558
that it's important to have
your parents with you on your wedding day.

297
00:20:36,401 --> 00:20:38,737
I owe him more than I can ever repay

298
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:42,491
because he granted every wish I ever had.

299
00:20:43,450 --> 00:20:44,993
So when he finally asked me

300
00:20:47,162 --> 00:20:48,789
for something,

301
00:20:50,832 --> 00:20:52,376
I couldn't say no

302
00:20:53,210 --> 00:20:54,836
because I know

303
00:20:56,713 --> 00:20:58,465
he would do anything.

304
00:21:10,852 --> 00:21:13,146
Your mom and dad
will walk you down the aisle.

305
00:22:00,736 --> 00:22:02,904
That gift you gave Chiara was incredible.

306
00:22:04,197 --> 00:22:06,158
I don't think I can top that.

307
00:22:10,370 --> 00:22:12,456
I had to pull every string I could.

308
00:22:17,669 --> 00:22:21,048
A temporary release
for Mr. and Mrs. Valtrovi?

309
00:22:21,131 --> 00:22:23,133
So they can attend Chiara's wedding?

310
00:22:24,468 --> 00:22:26,470
Yes. And I know you can help me.

311
00:22:28,263 --> 00:22:32,893
You and I both know
that arrangements like that

312
00:22:32,976 --> 00:22:37,647
are only approved
when an inmate loses a loved one

313
00:22:37,731 --> 00:22:43,612
or in a medical emergency
involving an immediate family member.

314
00:22:45,072 --> 00:22:49,576
That's exactly why I'm asking you.
I know you can make it happen.

315
00:22:52,120 --> 00:22:53,163
It's possible.

316
00:22:53,246 --> 00:22:59,169
I can justify it
under extraordinary circumstances,

317
00:22:59,252 --> 00:23:02,798
in case La Fornarina loses control again.

318
00:23:05,175 --> 00:23:06,676
And it's a good way

319
00:23:06,760 --> 00:23:09,721
to keep someone like Chiara Valtrovi
on the side of the law.

320
00:23:10,305 --> 00:23:12,349
And what will I gain from this?

321
00:23:17,896 --> 00:23:19,106
Just name your price.

322
00:23:20,899 --> 00:23:21,733
Anything?

323
00:23:27,697 --> 00:23:29,825
All right, then.

324
00:23:30,700 --> 00:23:33,161
I just want you to watch a movie with me.

325
00:23:38,083 --> 00:23:39,126
Which movie?

326
00:23:39,709 --> 00:23:40,752
Of course, a Lav Diaz film!

327
00:23:41,920 --> 00:23:43,213
Lav Diaz?

328
00:23:46,591 --> 00:23:48,260
You actually watched
a Lav Diaz movie with him?

329
00:23:49,136 --> 00:23:50,470
Wait, which one?

330
00:23:50,554 --> 00:23:53,014
<i>Evolution of a Filipino Family</i>.

331
00:23:53,098 --> 00:23:54,558
Evolution?

332
00:23:54,641 --> 00:23:57,185
Isn't that movie almost ten hours long?

333
00:24:00,522 --> 00:24:02,524
That's why one day,

334
00:24:02,607 --> 00:24:04,734
I'll make you pay me back.

335
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:10,740
Don't look at me like that.

336
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:13,618
We're even now.

337
00:24:17,789 --> 00:24:19,541
Thank you, Agent Alex.

338
00:24:20,917 --> 00:24:22,961
Thank you so, so much.

339
00:24:26,756 --> 00:24:28,633
What else are friends for?

340
00:24:54,367 --> 00:24:55,994
Thanks, Alex.

341
00:25:01,583 --> 00:25:03,627
And my very best friend!

342
00:25:18,391 --> 00:25:19,351
I'll get going.

343
00:25:27,442 --> 00:25:28,401
Take care!

344
00:25:36,326 --> 00:25:38,828
Come with me when I take a vacation.

345
00:25:38,912 --> 00:25:43,750
Europe is beautiful.
There’s a lot of good places to visit.

346
00:25:43,833 --> 00:25:45,794
You’re all about work!

347
00:25:47,045 --> 00:25:49,005
You’re just bald, Mr. Senator,

348
00:25:50,131 --> 00:25:54,052
but looks like
you’re not very clean at all.

349
00:25:56,346 --> 00:26:00,934
This photo is enough evidence
to investigate Senator Quintin.

350
00:26:01,017 --> 00:26:01,893
Are you sure?

351
00:26:02,477 --> 00:26:03,311
I’m sure.

352
00:26:03,395 --> 00:26:06,564
Shall we tell Sean or Agent Alex?

353
00:26:06,648 --> 00:26:07,899
What do you think?

354
00:26:08,692 --> 00:26:09,901
You know what? If you get stressed,

355
00:26:09,985 --> 00:26:12,112
you’ll get the same face as that.

356
00:26:14,322 --> 00:26:15,323
So harsh!

357
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:17,158
Be ready of my harsh version.

358
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:18,910
Because I will make her eat harsh browns.

359
00:26:20,495 --> 00:26:22,455
So what now? What should I do?

360
00:26:22,539 --> 00:26:24,332
Since we all have the same look,

361
00:26:26,501 --> 00:26:27,544
Come closer.

362
00:26:30,922 --> 00:26:32,007
Hey, Valtrovi!

363
00:26:32,090 --> 00:26:33,508
- You have a visitor.
- Who?

364
00:26:41,766 --> 00:26:43,268
Wouldn’t you ask me?
